You can use jrmc (the UI) or 

jrcmd 19846 X
 where X = start_recording 
         = stop_recording
	 = check_recording (to get a list of existing recordings)
	 = dump_recording id=record_id  copy_to_file=outputfilename

======

To have always-on profiling enabled run app as follows (can add other flags that you would use in jrcmd too)
java -XX:StartFlightRecording=filename=rec.jfr -jar dacapo-9.12-bach.jar eclipse

Later when you open-file this file in jrmc, look under CPU/Threads -> Hot Threads | Hot Methods.
Lock profiling requires separate enabling and usually comes at a cost IIUC

